    98	## 3. Expansion plan — where the ≈181,600 new words come from
    99	
   100	The source (≈118,400) is retold at roughly equal weight, plus ≈181,600 of new room. Every item serves the book promise (*make the reader feel the edge territories as the first place Cael has ever been fully free — and then make that freedom complicated*) or the arc (*no instrument out here reads me* → *nothing out here reads me, and the oldest thing out here stops every live Arbiter but leaves my fragments answering*). [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4, B7] Nothing below changes an end state or opens a reserved truth.
   101	
   102	1. **The brief cutaway system (+40,300, all new).** Five named companions-or-rivals at about 2.5–3% each, plus Vastin's single three-sentence window (§5). *Why:* the formula's ~13% secondary share. This book is also about *being priced*, so each window shows one of the people doing the pricing: the healer, the rival captain, the defector, the researcher, the partner.
   103	2. **The compressed roads and recoveries put on the page (+38,000).** The source summarizes the six days in the fin's lee and on the mountain's lip (+4k); the four days down to Oxhollow (+4k); the six days Oxhollow→Lowmarch (+4k); days 60–69 at Lowmarch and the well on the south road (+8k); the two days stone→Thornwater with Lira flat-footed (+3k); Thornwater→Lowmarch in the first cold (+2k); the three-day bearing walk (+4k); and the six days from the fourth site home in first snow (+5k). Thornwater's three stays get texture as a place that becomes home (+4k). *Why:* the arc's freedom is made of walking and of places that feed them, and the source keeps cutting it to a sentence.
   104	3. **The six-week skip and the first contracts on the page (+16,000).** The courier at the ford; falling in behind carters; Lowmarch's first week; the cart, the horse and the purse resolved (C1); the ferry escort, the fence-line and the wash as three short episodes; the meadow. *Why:* the source does all of this in a log. The edition's opening has to show the freedom before it complicates it, and to teach the board as a system.
   105	4. **The five set pieces given room (+26,000).** The ford (+4.5k), the stampede (+4.5k), the Ring (+6k, across two chapters), the Stair trap and ascent (+6k), and the Hall (+5k). *Why:* the owner's more-action direction. Each is a tactical problem new in kind (§8).
   106	5. **Learning encounters (+25,000).** Holding as a discipline ("the hold"): Lira running without the burst, Brom carrying without hardening, Karis keeping one point, Cael cataloguing his nine as held things with idle rents (+4k). Karis's discharge hypothesis tested (+1.5k). The shale-back study day (+2k). Oryn's field-care and two-readings teaching (+2.5k). The perimeter procedure and the six trials (+3k). The loft covenant (+1.5k). The listening cascade (+2k). The strata demonstration (+1.5k). The reading taught on the road (+1k). The wyrm trials (+2k). **New: Lira learns to shoot braced one-armed from Thornwater's bowman** during the week of tables (+4k). That plants Ch21, where "she could not span a bow one-armed… and could shoot one." *Why:* the formula's front-loaded teaching (§7), and so every winning mechanism is taught before it is used.
   107	6. **Supporting-cast arcs on the page (+12,000).** Private wants and independent decisions for Lira, Brom, Karis, Seln, Oryn, Teague and Pike, and small beats for the steading's woman, the bowman and Teague's crew (§6). Many small beats, no deuteragonist.
   108	7. **Seam repairs staged as scenes (+5,000).** The horse, cart and purse (C1). Oryn leaving her mule with the crew at Thornwater (C2). Karis pacing the Stair's perimeter on the morning of the 115th and laying the cord at the Hall on the 120th, so that Ch23's "paced two and cord-measured the third" is true on the page (C3).
   109	8. **Humor, warmth, letters and ledgers (+9,300).** The meadow; the jug; Lira's "In that order?"; the apples argument; Karis copying the wall she is kneeling on; the open-post habit; Pike's sayings at the book.
   110	9. **Retelling weight (+9,000).** The source's own scenes, rewritten at the formula's paragraph rhythm and given air, with no new events.
   111	
   112	**Do not add:** any new fight with stillhounds before the Ring, which would spend the Ring's surprise. Any Compact face, name, policy, directive or office scene beyond Vastin's window. Any new Shadow-adjacent use (it is used exactly twice: Ring, Stair). Any fragment use in M1–M3 beyond the ford's single burst (the log counts "Deployment since the Line: one" through day 90). Any Daeva or Reydan contact beyond one log line each. Any Ephram, Withrow, Rooke or Bracken scene (letters only). Any Coss, Havel or Ilsev. Any Teague-crew name.
