   271	**The log (Cael's entries; keep exact)**
   272	- Ch1 close: *Note the date. Season's open, and for once it isn't theirs.*
   273	- Ch2, the first pole: *No instrument out here reads me. No Arbiter station, no assessment panel, no registry seat with a seal on it. The board reads what we did. Since my Kindling I've been the case the instruments couldn't parse, and it turns out the cure was a country with no instruments. Write it plainly, because it's true: I'm free. First time.* [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
   274	- Ch3, the seal: *Seln did the shadow work tonight. I didn't. Out here there's a ledger and a ferry west once a month, and a defector's tradecraft in my hands would tell anyone who reads carefully where I learned it. The seal holds. Different country, same arithmetic.* — and *First honest number anyone's written about us in a year. It says four of five got hurt. It's right.*
   275	- Ch5 close: *The traverse holds. The map's good. Karis says the herd moves off declarations, which means the loudest thing on this mountain is us, and we've been quiet for five days. One more day. First honest job I've ever had that didn't have a fight at the end of it. Sleep.*
   276	- Ch6: *Eightieth day. Lira's leg is straight. The boxes are ours. The cart is in the gorge. A healer came up the road because a carter said we were late.*
   277	- Ch7: *Teague priced us. He's right about the cart. Oryn read me three times and got nothing three times and wants a fourth. Two people out here measuring me, and neither of them has a seal. I keep waiting to mind.*
   278	- Ch8, Part-1 summary (EXC-B7-001): *Twelve weeks. Seven contracts. Pike says there's ground out here where the Arbiter goes quiet, and nobody goes in twice. Karis has been waiting her whole life for a sentence like that. Seln says the contract was written by someone from inside. I say it pays. Two days east, through Thornwater, on the day the healer said. For twelve weeks nothing out here has read me. I'd like to see what a place that reads nothing does with that.*
   279	- Ch9, at the stone: *Quiet ground. Karis's Arbiter stopped at a line she can mark with a rock. So did Lira's, Brom's, Seln's, Oryn's — same line, same step. Mine didn't. Mine's been stopped since I was fourteen. I don't know what that means. Nobody asked. Tomorrow we go in.* [OWNER-pending #49]
   280	- Ch10: *The circle is perfect. The stakes are the registry's. The dogs are inside. Everyone's Path dies at the line and mine didn't, and I've told nobody, and I'm going to need to think about why I haven't. Not tonight. Tonight we're inside the one place on the continent where a stillhound can't lose.* [OWNER-pending #49]
   281	- Ch11, the Book 9 plant: *Everyone else's went to sleep at the stone. Mine has been asleep since I was fourteen. Out here that makes me the only one who's awake.* [OWNER-pending #49]
   282	- Ch12: *I'm not keeping it secret. I'm keeping it unfiled. There's a difference. Lira said later. Later is when I have a sentence. The answer might be: because whatever I am isn't a Path. I've known that since I was fourteen. Out there it was a flag. In there it's the only thing that works. I don't have a word for what that makes me, and I'm not going to invent one at a camp with Lira's arm two hours old.* [OWNER-pending #49]
   283	- Ch13, the covenant, whole: *Written before. Tomorrow morning, the back room, the door shut. Oryn runs the long reading. Both hands, all of her, all of me, twenty minutes. I lie still. I'm still and whole for the first time in front of her; she said so in the yard, with the tape off.* / *The conditions, as I have them. Sustained: twenty minutes at contact is longer than any bout I've stood. Stakes: I'm three days off the Ring and the nine are still settling; she's three mendings down and her route's late at the far end and she's spending a fourth on a patient who's given her nothing four times. Earnest: she'll do the thing she does as well as she does it. Karis: the model says real, not fight. I don't know if the model's right. Nobody does. Tomorrow's the first time it could be tested and I'm the test.* / *The price. She doesn't know what I am. She can't consent to what she can't know about — not won't; can't. There's nothing I could put in front of her tonight that she could say yes or no to, because the thing doesn't have a name she's heard. I've decided not to tell her before. My reasons are good, and they're the reasons of somebody who wants it, and the real one is that I don't know what she'd say. Entered.* / *If it takes what she's using on me, it takes it from the one person on this road who came to help. I don't know what it costs a source. It's never shown. Tomorrow's the first time it could, and if it does, she pays, and I chose that for her.* / *After: I tell her. In full. On her table, before I'm off it. Whatever it costs me, including the route walking north without me on it.* / *I want it. Write that too.* / *Write it before, not after. That's the whole difference between me and the system.*
   284	- Ch14, the birthday line: *Hundred and second day past the Line. Nineteen. Written at Thornwater, in the steading's common room, the fire lit for us. Witnesses: four of my own, and a healer who's a stop.* [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: OWNER-pending #48]
   285	- Ch14, the words retired: *Still open. Still real. Now I can see it. That's worse. The tenth fragment lets me feel my own currents, and there's one in the place session nine logged, and it isn't the tenth, and it isn't any of the nine. It was there before Oryn. It was there before Brom's read caught it. I don't know what it is. I know where it is now. Patience is over; observation begins.* — and *Daeva's rematch, Reydan's answer — both ride east. Nineteen. Ten fragments. Hesk's package is on a ferry somewhere. The last one said mind the shape. I'm starting to.*
   286	- Ch16, the rule: *The reading turned outward. I ask first. Every time. If I ever don't, that's the day I became the instrument.*
   287	- Ch16, the second pole: *Nothing out here reads me. And at a line you can mark with a rock, every Path in this camp stops, and mine doesn't. Karis won't write her hypothesis. I won't write mine. We're going to find the other circles. Pike said nobody goes in twice. Tomorrow makes three.* [OWNER-pending #49]
   288	- Ch17 (EXC-B7-002): *Priced too well. Seln says it's for the case. I say the floor's for me and they don't know it. South, tomorrow. Lira's arm is two weeks old. Brom says doors open both ways. He's quoting Rooke. He's never quoted anyone.*
   289	- Ch18: *Hundred and thirteenth day, the fork above Millrace. Oryn came. On her terms. She'll turn north the day she has to and I won't ask her not to.*
   290	- Ch19: *Second nameless team. Same hand. I own a piece of the first one and I used it on the second. The account's still unpayable. It's getting longer.*
   291	- Ch20: *Instruments recovered. The contract's paid, and the man who posted it is never going to see them, because Seln's keeping the ledger and I'm keeping the kit. Someone measured this place five years ago and wrote bearing and stopped. Karis has a straightedge. She's been waiting her whole life to use it. The Ring, the Stair, and whatever's on that bearing. Pike said a handful. We have two. The kit says three. We're going to go look.*
   292	- Ch22, the still place: *Read myself. Ten currents, and I can't find the banks either — Oryn's right. And the anomaly's there. Not a fragment. Not a flow. A still place, and the rest of me has been going around it since before I knew it existed. It isn't the Quiet. The Quiet is outside me and turns Paths off. This is inside me and the Paths — the fragments — go around it like they were built to. I don't know what it is. I know it was there before Oryn, before Brom's read, before the ring. Session nine caught the edge of it. I'm not going to guess. Guessing is what the registry did to me. Observation, then the log, then patience.*
   293	- Ch22, the stake paid: *Teague sat down next to me. Asked what I am. I could have read him. I asked instead. The day I stop asking is the day I'm the registry. Write it down. Again. Every time.*
   294	- Ch23: *Hundred and twenty-second day, the fork. Oryn north. On her terms. I didn't ask. Five on the bearing.* — *I love this country.* — and the crest: *Four sites. One line. The last one's twice the size and the Compact fenced it. The bearing runs through it and keeps going. Karis says four points is an argument. I say it's a bearing — the kind their maps draw as nothing. Home is Lowmarch now. I just wrote that without noticing. Nineteen, ten fragments, a still place at the center of me, and a line on a map that somebody drew before there were maps. We're not done. We're oriented.*
   295	- Ch24, the inventory: *Ten confirmed fragments.* / *Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — the Bronze from Ardenmere. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — Seln; source protected; the seal held past the Line as it held inside, and was used twice out here where no one who could carry it west could see it, and that is the seal's whole logic and it is unchanged. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; opened a door on a rim and held a floor in a hall, and I own a piece of the craft the system uses to hold people and have used it twice this year, once each way. Blade-adjacent — Ephram. Tide-adjacent — Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; the tenth, and the first that does nothing in a fight, and the only one whose engagement field says clinical, and the only one with a rule on it in her hand and mine: ask first, every time. Deployment notes current on all ten.* / *One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.* / *Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. Both are going to need a map.* — **Audio rule:** Feryn's name never appears in a list run beside Oryn's; every inventory says "the Bronze from Ardenmere."
