   166	
   167	*In hand, nine.*
   168	
   169	*Deployment since the Line: none.*
   170	
   171	Lira had come to sit by him, with her arms round her knees. She had read it over his arm, as she always did, and she said nothing about it for some time.
   172	
   173	"Thirteenth of thirteen," she said at last. "Sent for the forty. Do you know what that would be, at home? It'd be the bottom seed drawn against the title in the first round, because the title was out of town. Iron against Gold, and no panel to tell you so."
   174	
   175	"It isn't a draw."
   176	
   177	"No. That's what I can't get used to. Nobody put us against it. He just said it was there." She rubbed her nose. "I keep wanting to know the odds. There's nobody making any."
   178	
   179	"Would it help?"
   180	
   181	"It always did. You know where you are when somebody's bet against you." She unfolded her legs and stood. "You're the fifth tonight, so go to sleep. It's in the table."
