editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-12.md:89:Cael had not known that he ever did. He walked across the yard in his slow dry way with a length of ash in his hand, peeled, as tall as his shoulder, with a fork left at the top of it for a palm to sit in, and he stood it against the trough where Lira's hand would find it. He kept his eyes off her foot. He lifted two fingers from his side, an inch, and let them fall, and went back up his ladder.
